    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000148664119": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Research Engagement Manager",
      "description": "University of Auckland Research Engagement Manager - 4 positions (Aligned to the University's Signature Research Areas) | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Research Engagement Manager - 4 positions (Aligned to the University's Signature Research Areas) Full-time Campus: Newmarket Campus Position Number: 60020685 UoA Department Name: Research Development and Impact Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland creates globally transformative impacts through its distinctive strengths in world-leading research, scholarship, teaching and collaborative partnerships, inspired by its unique position in Aotearoa New Zealand and the Asia-Pacific. Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We are seeking Three Research Engagement Managers to join a newly established Research Engagement function within Te Puna Tiketike | Research and Innovation Office. These newly created roles will play a pivotal role in building strategic partnerships, facilitating collaboration between researchers and external stakeholders, and helping shape research agendas that deliver meaningful impact for communities, industry, government and society. Working across the University's Signature Research Areas, you will contribute to a transformative approach to research engagement that strengthens research excellence, innovation and impact. As a dedicated relationship manager, facilitator and strategic connector, you will bring together internal and external partners to foster collaboration, build trusted relationships, and support the development of impactful research initiatives. The role is focused on identifying opportunities, building partnerships, facilitating co-design processes, and helping position the University as a partner of choice across diverse stakeholder communities. Four exciting opportunities across our Signature Research Areas We are recruiting Four Research Engagement Managers, with each role aligned to one of the University's Signature Research Areas (SRAs). These areas bring together interdisciplinary expertise to address some of the most significant challenges and opportunities facing Aotearoa New Zealand and the world. The available areas are: Frontier Technologies Ancestral Futures Blue Pacific Horizons The Energy Movement To learn more about the University's Signature Research Areas, please visit: https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/research/signature-research-areas.html Key responsibilities include: Provide specialist advice to Signature Research Area (SRA) research leads and University Research Centre (URC) Directors on engagement strategy, partnership development, and co-design practice. Embed structured impact practice, including theory of change and implementation-informed approaches, into engagement planning so that impact pathways are shaped from the earliest stages of partnership formation. Build and steward long-term, mutually beneficial relationships across industry, funders, government, civil society, and international partners. Act as a strategic broker and wayfinder, connecting external partners to relevant University expertise and applied innovation capability. Identify opportunities to elevate the profile of University research, researchers, and strategic research priorities through coordinated engagement, thought leadership, stakeholder events, and strategic communications. This is a Permanent full‑time, 37.5‑hour‑per‑week contract.  This is a band H role with a salary range from $98,700 pa to $121,900 pa. This position will be based at the Newmarket Campus For more information on the role, please view the Position Description. About the Research Engagement Team We're establishing a new Research Engagement function within Te Puna Tiketike | Research and Innovation Office to strengthen the University's ability to build meaningful, long-term partnerships that enable excellent research and deliver impact. Working alongside researchers, communities, iwi, industry, government and other partners, the team will help shape shared research agendas, foster transdisciplinary collaboration, and support co-designed research that addresses challenges of national and global importance. Rather than responding to opportunities as they arise, the team will take a strategic, relationship-centred approach to engagement, helping position the University as a trusted partner and making it easier for external organisations to connect with our research expertise. Aligned to the University's Signature Research Areas, the team will work closely with researchers to develop enduring partnerships, build engagement capability across the University, and embed research engagement and impact as core components of research excellence. He kōrero mōu | About you You are a strategic relationship-builder who thrives in complex environments and enjoys bringing people, ideas and opportunities together. You are confident engaging with a wide range of stakeholders and can balance long-term relationship development with achieving meaningful outcomes. Skills and experience that are required: A tertiary qualification aligned to a Signature Research Area, or equivalent professional expertise within a relevant research domain. Experience in research engagement, research partnerships, strategic stakeholder engagement, knowledge mobilisation, or a related field. Demonstrated success building and sustaining trusted, mutually beneficial relationships with diverse stakeholders. Strong facilitation skills and experience bringing together stakeholders to shape shared priorities and outcomes. The ability to take initiative, exercise sound judgement and work autonomously in a complex, multi-stakeholder environment. Excellent communication and influencing skills, with the ability to engage credibly with researchers, senior leaders, industry, government and community partners. Additional Information Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland - is New Zealand's leading university and offers an excellent working environment through: Flexible employment practices Up to 6.75% employer superannuation contribution Five weeks' annual leave Career development and professional learning opportunities Generous parental leave provisions Excellent campus facilities Access to a range of staff benefits, wellbeing initiatives, and discounts For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online by the closing date of 22nd of September 2026 (NZST) to be considered. Please include your CV and a cover letter outlining how your skills and experience align with the requirements of the role. As part of your application, please indicate in your Cover letter which Signature Research Area your expertise, qualifications and experience best align with, as each Research Engagement Manager role will support a dedicated Signature Research Area. For any questions related to the role, please reach out to the Kristiann Allen on kristiann.allen@auckland.ac.nz Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Lecturer in European Studies, with Gender Studies Auckland, New Zealand Research Engagement Manager - Māori Auckland, New Zealand Executive Communications Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Research Engagement Manager - 4 positions (Aligned to the University's Signature Research Areas) Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000148639313": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Inspera Casual",
      "description": "University of Auckland Inspera Casual  | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Inspera Casual Casual Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60016371 UoA Department Name: Student and Academic Services Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading University. With over 6000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are one of NZ’s largest employers. Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity Assessment Services is fast approaching one of our busiest times of the year with semester two exams just around the corner. We are seeking to employ enthusiastic and results-driven casual staff members to support online exams and provide in class student support. Applicants must be technically minded and be able to explain technical concepts to students and staff in an exam setting. You must also have an excellent eye for detail and meticulous in your record keeping. You need to be available for training in the week of the 19th of October to the 23rd of October and from the 29th of October until the 16th of November will be full-time hours (Monday - Friday 8.30am/9am - 4pm/5.30pm). You will need to be confident using online systems and talking through processes to new and existing users. You'll also need great communication skills to manage queries with patience, professionalism and confidence. Skills you will bring to the role: Proven experience in a customer focused role Strong communication skills Digitally savvy and confident using technology Keen to learn in a fast-paced environment with the ability to pick up new information promptly. Responsibilities include: Assisting with setting up exams and assessments in Inspera. Providing technical support for professional and academic staff across the University. Providing ad hoc user support as needed. Tracking exam and assessment set-up in Inspera, stepping in to assist when required. Provide subject matter expertise and support. Assist with class test, assessment organisation and delivery using Inspera. Performing quality checks before exams and assessments go live to students. Monitor progress of tests and exams online. This is a casual role. The hourly rate for this role is $29 per hour. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer The University of Auckland is New Zealand's leading University and maintains significant computational, laboratory, and analytic facilities. Auckland is frequently rated as one of the world's most liveable cities. The University is committed to providing an excellent working environment through the following: Flexible employment practices (including working from home and flexible hours) Up to 6.75% company superannuation scheme A competitive salary with five weeks' annual leave In addition, we also offer career development programs, discounted car parking, a generous parental leave allowance, childcare, and other discounts on internal and external services. For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online by the closing date of 18/09/2026 to be considered. Please include your cover letter and CV highlighting how you can meet the abovementioned skills and experiences. Please note that we may close the advert earlier if we find a suitable candidate. Please reach out to Sarah Puett - sarah.puett@auckland.ac.nz for a confidential conversation. Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. #LI-DNI Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Student Hub Assistant Auckland, New Zealand Assessment Integrity Support Auckland, New Zealand Lecturer in European Studies, with Gender Studies Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Inspera Casual Auckland, New Zealand Casual I'm interested I'm interested"
