    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000147415929": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor",
      "description": "University of Auckland Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor - Inclusive Education  | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor - Inclusive Education Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60020826 UoA Department Name: Education and Social Practice Company Description Job Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland creates globally transformative impacts through its distinctive strengths in world-leading research, scholarship, teaching and collaborative partnerships, inspired by its unique position in Aotearoa New Zealand and the Asia-Pacific. Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity The School of Education and Social Practice within Te Pūtahi Mātauranga | Faculty of Arts and Education is seeking a Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor in Inclusive Education to join our collegial academic team. This is an opportunity to contribute to teaching, research and service across Inclusive Education, including undergraduate, initial teacher education and postgraduate programmes. You will develop and lead programmes of research, contribute to curriculum development and postgraduate supervision, and build collaborative relationships with schools, policymakers and the wider educational community. A key responsibility of the role will be to serve as Programme Director for the postgraduate specialisation in Inclusive Education. The specialisation develops advanced knowledge and capability in inclusive practices to support diverse learners in educational settings, equipping graduates to influence inclusive policies and practices within their organisations. Key responsibilities include: Delivering high-quality teaching, contributing to curriculum development and supervising postgraduate research students. Developing and leading high-quality research programmes in Inclusive Education, including scholarly publications, research collaborations and external funding opportunities. Providing programme and academic leadership as Programme Director for the postgraduate Inclusive Education specialisation, alongside Course Directorship and School and Faculty service. Building and maintaining positive partnerships with schools, policymakers and the wider educational community. This is a full-time (40 hours per week) permanent position (subject to continuation). The workload split is 40% teaching, 40% research, and 20% service. Remuneration will be determined based on experience and achievements, in accordance with our Academic Standards policy . The salary ranges are: Senior Lecturer: $126,863 – $158,904 per annum Associate Professor: from $165,808 per annum For more detailed information on the role accountabilities and requirements, please review the Position Description. He kōrero mōu | About you You are a recognised expert in Inclusive Education with a strong record of impactful research and a passion for developing inclusive practice across education settings. You bring deep knowledge of Inclusive Education policies, pedagogies and practices, together with the leadership capability to contribute to teaching, research and programme development. To be successful in this role, you will bring: A PhD in Inclusive Education or a related field. Experience teaching undergraduate and postgraduate courses in Inclusive Education. A strong record of high-quality and impactful publications in Inclusive Education. Deep knowledge of Inclusive Education policies, pedagogies and practices. Proven experience as an engaging and effective teacher, with leadership experience in a tertiary environment. Strong communication, collaboration and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work effectively with teachers, schools, policymakers and community partners. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer As New Zealand’s largest, highest ranked and most comprehensive research intensive university, we are committed to supporting your career with: Excellent research, teaching, and campus facilities Generous Research & Study Leave Full range of research and leadership development programmes For more information, please visit Staff Benefits. Auckland is a vibrant cosmopolitan and growing city with a population of 1.8m (greater Auckland area). The University is located in the metropolitan centre and commercial heart of Aotearoa New Zealand. We have an abundance of natural features, including four stunning harbours, accessible coastline, native bush and moderate temperatures, which help us retain our reputation as one of the best cities in the world to live. Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online by the closing date of Wednesday 23rd September to be considered. Please include your CV and a cover letter outlining your interest in and suitability for the role. Please direct enquiries to Fiona Ell (Associate Head of School) via [email protected] . Please note while we are happy to answer your questions, we do not accept applications via email. Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000147411099": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Facilities & Services Team Leader",
      "description": "University of Auckland Facilities & Services Team Leader | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Facilities & Services Team Leader Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60004330 UoA Department Name: Business and Economics Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We are currently seeking an experienced and highly organised Facilities & Services Team Leader to join the aligned professional staff services between the Faculty of Business and Faculty of Law. This is a varied and rewarding leadership role that combines people management, office administration, operational planning, reporting, project coordination, and service delivery. You will play a key role in ensuring the smooth day-to-day operation of the two Faculties while leading a team dedicated to delivering high-quality support services. Based primarily at the Faculty of Law on, Eden Crescent City Campus, you will work closely with stakeholders across both the Faculty of Law and the Business School. The role requires some travelling between the Business School and the Law school. Leading 2 Facility Coordinators, Reception Staff and Interns  you will provide leadership, guidance, and operational oversight to ensure an excellent experience for staff, students, and visitors. Key responsibilities include: Leading, coaching, and developing a small team to deliver outstanding customer service and operational support Managing the day-to-day delivery of administration, and facilities services Coordinating workloads, priorities, and resources to ensure service standards are met Preparing reports, presentations, professional correspondence, and operational documentation Generating and analysing information to support planning, decision-making, and continuous improvement initiatives Supporting and coordinating operational projects and service improvement activities Facilitating meetings and ensuring follow-up actions are completed Managing procurement activities, supplier relationships, and resource allocation Liaising with Property Services regarding maintenance, facilities issues, and operational requirements Building strong relationships with academic and professional staff across the University Supporting health, safety, business continuity, and operational planning activities Identifying opportunities to improve processes and enhance service delivery This is a full-time (37.5 hours per week), fixed-term position till December 2027, while a review of resourcing is undertaken. Working hours: Monday to Friday, 8:00am to 4:00pm. This is a Band F professional staff role with a salary range of $73,400 - $90,700 per annum, dependent on qualifications, skills, and experience. For more information about the role, please review position description. Mō tō mātou rōpū | About the team Based within the Faculty of Law, this role sits within a Facilities Services team that works across both the Faculty of Law and the Faculty of Business and Economics, creating opportunities to build relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders. The team is responsible for delivering high-quality administration, operational, and facilities support services that enable staff and students to thrive in a welcoming and well-managed environment. He kōrero mōu | About you We are looking for a confident and capable operational leader who is passionate about supporting both people and processes to succeed. To be successful in this role, you will have: Demonstrated experience leading and developing a small team Strong office administration, operations, business support, or service delivery experience Excellent written communication skills, including the ability to prepare reports, correspondence, procedures, and business documentation Experience generating, analysing, and presenting reports to support operational decision-making Strong project management or project coordination experience Excellent organisational and planning skills, with strong attention to detail The ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment Strong stakeholder relationship management and communication skills A customer-focused mindset with a commitment to delivering exceptional service Sound judgement, initiative, and problem-solving capabilities Experience managing procurement processes, vendors, or service providers Advanced proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications, particularly Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams, and PowerPoint Additional Information Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland - is New Zealand's leading university and offers an excellent working environment through: Five weeks' annual leave pro rate Career development and professional learning opportunities Excellent campus facilities Access to a range of staff benefits, wellbeing initiatives, and discounts For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online by the closing date of Friday 18th of September 2026 to be considered. Please include your cover letter and CV highlighting how your skills and experience align with this opportunity. For any questions related to the role please contact Himendra Ratnayake on h.ratnayake@auckland.ac.nz Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Functional Analyst Manager Auckland, New Zealand Team Leader, Student Hubs and Client Services Auckland, New Zealand Lecturer in Sport Health & Physical Education Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Facilities & Services Team Leader Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000147409159": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Media Adviser",
      "description": "University of Auckland Media Adviser | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Media Adviser Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60019614 UoA Department Name: Communications Job Description With more than 47,000 students and over 6,000 staff, Waipapa Taumata Rau is New Zealand's leading university and a globally connected organisation dedicated to creating knowledge, transforming lives and shaping futures. As part of our newly established Communications function, we're investing in the future of communications practice. Find out more about the ways we are transforming how we engage with our internal and external audiences across our Marketing, Recruitment, Communications and Engagement functions. Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity At Waipapa Taumata Rau, University of Auckland, our research, teaching and people are helping shape the future of Aotearoa New Zealand and beyond. We're looking for a talented Media Adviser to help share those stories. This is an exciting opportunity for a communications, journalism or media relations professional who enjoys uncovering compelling stories, building strong media relationships, and contributing to the reputation of one of New Zealand's most recognised and respected institutions. You'll play a key role in promoting the University's research, teaching excellence, student success and societal impact through proactive media engagement and external communications. Working closely with academics, researchers, professional staff and communications colleagues, you'll identify stories that deserve attention, transform complex ideas into compelling content, and connect journalists with the experts and insights they need. Key areas of focus: Develop and pitch stories that build the University's profile, reputation and influence Write media releases, media responses, key messages and external communications content Build strong working relationships with journalists, editors and media outlets Identify opportunities to showcase research breakthroughs, student success stories and institutional achievements Prepare briefing materials and support University spokespeople for media engagement Monitor media coverage, emerging issues and sector trends Contribute to integrated external communications activity across traditional, digital, social media and emerging channels Support communications activity during significant issues, incidents or high-profile events This is a full-time, permanent opportunity. The full salary range for this role is $87,000 - $118,000 per annum We have a structured salary framework with three zones for those developing into the role (developing), fully effective (target) and contributing beyond what is expected of the role (upper). Appointments are typically made within the target range of $93,201 – $107,500 per annum, depending on skills, experience, and internal equity. We welcome conversations about your expectations and what matters to you in your overall package. Any offer will be made within the advertised range and guided by fairness, consistency, and our commitment to pay equity . For more detailed information about the role and requirements, please refer to the position description He kōrero mōu | About you You'll be a curious and collaborative communications professional with a passion for great storytelling. We're particularly interested in people who bring: Outstanding writing and storytelling skills Experience developing media content and communications materials Strong relationship-building and stakeholder management capability Sound judgement and professionalism when dealing with sensitive issues Experience in complex organisations An interest in digital and emerging communications channels Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer Our scale creates opportunities that few organisations can offer. From research and innovation to education, reputation and community engagement, you'll work across a diverse range of communications challenges while contributing to initiatives that have real and lasting impact for staff, students, our communities and the world. Beyond the work itself, you'll be joining a vibrant and inclusive community. From staff networks and cultural communities to social clubs, volunteering opportunities, wellbeing initiatives and campus events, there are countless ways to connect, contribute and build meaningful relationships across the University. We also offer: A commitment to work/life balance with a 37.5 hour working week, flexible hours and hybrid/remote working patterns A competitive remuneration package with up to 6.75% super, annual salary increase with performance-based multiplier Time to recharge and disconnect with 5 weeks' annual leave and additional leave buy/sell scheme Support for parents and carers with subsidised on-site childcare (including Kōhanga Reo), gender-neutral parental leave with up to 9 weeks’ full pay, on-site parenting and feeding spaces A commitment to the wellbeing of our people with confidential access to a range of EAP services, including mental health counselling, financial guidance, neurodiversity coaching and rongoā services, a world-class on-site fitness centre, access to student specialists across our supervised training clinics, discounted health insurance The opportunity to grow with access to an extensive programme of professional, leadership and cultural development, including digital capability coaching, specialised leadership development programmes, and Te Ao and Te Reo Māori learning programmes for staff The opportunity to build your career with one of New Zealand's most diverse and complex organisations Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Please submit an application online by the closing date of 3 October 2026. Please include your cover letter and your CV highlighting your interest in the role, your capabilities and relevant experience. Reasonable accommodations - We are committed to building a more equitable and inclusive workforce and workplace, so we encourage applicants to reach out to discuss any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process, including alternative ways to submit applications. Whānau and support people - Should you be invited to an interview for this role, your whānau members and/or support people will be welcome to join you. The recruiter or hiring manager will provide more information about this as part of the interview arrangements. Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Admissions Manager Auckland, New Zealand Exam Supervisor - Special Auckland, New Zealand Associate Director, Performance and Digital Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Media Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
