    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000150928619": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Senior Clinics Administrator",
      "description": "University of Auckland Senior Clinics Administrator | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Senior Clinics Administrator Full-time Campus: Grafton Campus Position Number: 00016361 UoA Department Name: Technical Services Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading University. With over 6000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are one of NZ’s largest employers.  We have six academic faculties, two large-scale research institutes and a number of professional service divisions creating a diverse, dynamic and complex organisational culture that demands excellence. Our lecturers and researchers are regarded as experts in their fields, frequently directing global research projects designed to better the lives of New Zealanders and the world, and in turn passing this knowledge on to our students. Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We are seeking an enthusiastic Senior Clinic Administrator to support the University of Auckland Optometry Clinic within the Faculty of Medical and Health Sciences. You will play a vital role in the day-to-day operations of our student-led teaching clinic. This role is responsible for patient support, administration, reception, and the daily activities that keep our busy and diverse clinic running smoothly. Supporting our Optometry Clinic, you'll enjoy a variety of tasks, work with a diverse patient population, and be part of a unique environment that delivers high-quality clinical services while helping students achieve the clinical competencies required for course completion. In essence, you'll be helping to support the training and development of the future allied health workforce. Key responsibilities include Front-of-house and reception responsibilities. Liaising with patients and providing information about our services. Appointment scheduling and diary management across multiple user groups. Invoice processing and payment collection. Processing external claims. Managing Healthlink referrals to Health NZ and other external agencies. Ensuring patient confidentiality protocols and requirements are adhered to. Obtaining and maintaining appropriate consent and documentation prior to service delivery. Supporting clinical teams with the preparation and distribution of clinical correspondence. Maintaining Health and Safety standards in line with University and legislative requirements. This is a fulltime, permanent position The salary range for this role is $61,701 - $71,000 depending on skills and experience. For more detailed information, please refer to the position description He kōrero mōu | About you You'll have experience in a busy administration, reception or customer-facing role and enjoy working in a fast-paced environment where no two days are the same. In addition, you'll bring: Previous experience in the health sector would be advantageous. Experience processing financial transactions. Experience using patient management systems or similar databases. Experience supporting multiple Optometry services or comparable clinical environments. Strong proficiency across the Microsoft Office suite. A professional and confident phone manner. Excellent organisational skills and a strong commitment to providing outstanding service. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer The University of Auckland is committed to providing an excellent working environment through: Flexible employment practices and a culture that supports work-life balance Career development programmes A competitive salary with five weeks’ annual leave 6.75% superannuation scheme For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications should be submitted online, before the closing date of 2 October and include an up-to-date CV and cover letter outlining what strengths you will bring to this role. If you have any questions, please email Clivenn Naepi via Clivenn.naepi@auckland.ac.nz Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications via email #LI-DNI Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Digital & Lifecycle Content Specialist Auckland, New Zealand Research Operations Coordinator Auckland, New Zealand Casual Study Doctor – Neurogenetics Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Senior Clinics Administrator Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000151559199": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Product Manager",
      "description": "University of Auckland Product Manager - Enterprise AI | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Product Manager - Enterprise AI Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60015409 UoA Department Name: Experience Innovation Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We are seeking a Product Manager - Enterprise AI to lead the University's vision, strategy and roadmap for Artificial Intelligence. This role will play a critical part in shaping how AI is adopted and applied across the University, ensuring investments deliver measurable value while aligning with the University's AI Action Plan, governance frameworks and digital strategy. Working across business domains, digital delivery teams, data specialists, architecture, security and senior stakeholders, you will identify opportunities where AI can improve services, decision-making and operational efficiency. You will take ownership of the AI product lifecycle, from discovery and business case development through to implementation, governance, measurement and continuous improvement. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced Product Manager to help define the future of AI at the University. You will be responsible for balancing innovation with responsible delivery, ensuring AI initiatives are supported by strong data governance, appropriate security controls, clear outcomes and robust return on investment. While you will not develop AI models directly, you will work closely with technical teams to translate business challenges into AI-enabled solutions that are practical, scalable and trustworthy. Your responsibilities will include: Developing and maintaining the University's AI vision, roadmap and product strategy Leading the prioritisation and lifecycle management of AI-enabled products and services Partnering with architecture, security, data and delivery teams to ensure AI solutions are scalable, secure and governed appropriately Building business cases and evaluating opportunities based on value, cost, risk and measurable outcomes Engaging and influencing stakeholders across the University to drive adoption and understanding of AI initiatives Promoting best practice in responsible AI, data governance and ethical decision-making This is a 24-month fixed-term, full-time position (37.5 hours per week). The salary range for this role is $135,000 to $155,000 , negotiable depending on skills and experience. A full description of your duties and the role are provided in the position description linked HERE He kōrero mōu | About you You are an experienced Product Manager who enjoys working at the intersection of strategy, technology and business outcomes. You have a strong understanding of AI and machine learning concepts and can confidently assess opportunities, risks and value propositions associated with AI-enabled solutions. You are comfortable leading conversations around governance, security, architecture, data quality and return on investment, and can translate complex technical concepts into clear business outcomes. You bring a collaborative approach, strong stakeholder management skills, and experience guiding products through their full lifecycle, from discovery and prioritisation through to delivery and continuous improvement. You are equally comfortable working with senior leaders, business owners, architects, security teams and technical specialists, helping align diverse perspectives around a shared vision and measurable outcomes. E rapua ana mātou | We are seeking Significant experience in Product Management, Product Ownership or a similar strategic leadership role within a large and complex organisation Strong understanding of AI and machine learning concepts, including governance, risk, security and responsible AI practices Experience developing product roadmaps, business cases and investment priorities that deliver measurable outcomes and return on investment Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional initiatives and build alignment across business, data, architecture, security and delivery teams Strong stakeholder engagement and communication skills, with the ability to influence senior leaders and translate technical concepts into business value Experience managing the full product lifecycle, including discovery, prioritisation, delivery, governance and continuous improvement Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading university, guided by a commitment to excellence and service to our communities. With more than 6,000 academic and professional staff, we support a diverse community of over 47,000 students. Guided by our values , we work collaboratively to advance knowledge, foster equity and inclusion, and contribute meaningfully to New Zealand’s social, cultural, and economic well-being. We cultivate an environment that supports your growth and rewards excellence with a range of staff benefits , including: Competitive salary and five weeks of annual leave Discounted public Transport for permanent and long-term fixed term staff Superannuation/KiwiSaver , matching up to 6.75% Flexible working arrangements, including working from home and flexible hours Leading, and inclusive parental leave provisions Career development opportunities and a range of benefits, including discounted insurance , memberships , and on‑site amenities Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Please submit your application online by the closing date of Sunday, 11 October 2026 . Your application should include: A brief Cover Letter explaining why you're interested in this role and how your skills match the requirements. Your updated CV . Please note that we do not accept email applications. For a confidential discussion, you are welcome to contact Neil Gardner, Senior Recruitment Consultant, neil.gardner@auckland.ac.nz Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Digital & Lifecycle Content Specialist Auckland, New Zealand Functional Analyst Manager Auckland, New Zealand Development Manager - Fundraising Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Product Manager - Enterprise AI Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000151545749": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Student Support Advisor",
      "description": "University of Auckland Student Support Advisor | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Student Support Advisor Full-time Campus: Grafton Campus Position Number: 60017198 UoA Department Name: Te Kupenga Hauora Maori Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The Faculty of Medical and Health Sciences is a diverse faculty with more than 4,000 students studying across six schools, led by world-leading researchers, teachers, and practising health professionals.  Our Vision is to lead and advance Hauora across generations in Aotearoa courageously.  As such, we are committed to leading and advancing the mana of Aotearoa as a global centre of Health learning, research, and innovation. Te Kupenga Hauora Māori (TKHM) is located at the Grafton Campus. TKHM represents the Department of Māori Health and is responsible for the coordination of Māori health teaching across the Faculty of Medical and Health Sciences, the Vision 20:20 initiative responsible for Indigenous health workforce development, and the Tōmaiora Research Unit is responsible for conducting Kaupapa Māori health research and training services. Located on the Grafton Campus, the school is fully self-contained, in a purpose-built building. The building has been designed to maximise interaction and collaboration. Our knowledge, expertise and teaching are our taonga. We value our students, alumni and donors. We work closely with partners such as Te Whatu Ora | Health NZ and Te Aka Whai Ora | Māori Health Authority, as well as communities, organisations, industry and international partners to advance the well-being of the people of Aotearoa, with a clear commitment to sustainably regenerate people & place. Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | About the Role To fulfil our commitment to the Vision 20:20 initiative, which aims to increase the number of Māori and Pacific health professionals through the Māori and Pacific Admission Scheme (MAPAS). TKHM seeks to recruit an inspiring individual to support our Māori and Pacific students through their cultural and educational journey within the Faculty of Medical and Health Sciences (FMHS) as the Student Support Advisor The kaupapa of this role is: coordinating academic and pastoral support for Māori and Pacific students who are studying in either foundation, undergraduate or postgraduate programmes responsible for the administration, management and coordination of admission, academic, and pastoral support for our students. This is an excellent opportunity to undertake responsibility and be innovative in a stimulating position that demands critical thinking as well as a practical approach. Mō tō mātou rōpū | About the team Our team pride themselves on our positive working environment, where we work collaboratively to develop innovative solutions. We work closely and are always committed to giving and accepting feedback to ensure we provide the best service possible to our students. He kōrero mōu | About you The successful candidate will have an well-developed/in-depth understanding of Māori and Pacific culture to provide support, advice and mentorship to students throughout their journey with us and will have strong connections to Māori and/or Pacific communities. In addition, you will: Understand the challenges Māori and Pacific students encounter while studying at university Have a relevant undergraduate degree Be able to work independently as well as within a team Have a high competency in administration and communication skills Have a demonstrated ability to build effective relationships Have an ability to coordinate and manage events Be able to collaborate and work in partnership with key academic staff Have excellent time management and organisational skills Be flexible and able to work evenings and weekends This position is fulltime , fixed term for 18 months and the salary range is $63,600 - $79,300 (pro rata), dependent on skills and experience. For further information please refer to the Position Description Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading university and maintains significant computational, laboratory and analytic facilities. Auckland itself is frequently rated as one of the world’s most liveable cities. The University is committed to providing an excellent working environment through: Flexible employment practices (including working from home, flexible hours) A competitive salary with five weeks’ annual leave In addition, we also offer career development programmes, discounted car parking, a generous parental leave allowance, childcare, and a number of other discounts on internal and external services. For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online by the closing date of 26/09/2026 to be considered. Please include your cover letter and CV highlighting how you can meet the above-mentioned skills and experiences. Please reach out to Sue Reddy via sue.reddy@auckland.ac.nz for a confidential conversation. Please note that we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Development Manager - Fundraising Auckland, New Zealand Product Manager - Enterprise AI Auckland, New Zealand Digital & Lifecycle Content Specialist Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Student Support Advisor Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000151525599": {
      "title": "Digital & Lifecycle Content Specialist",
      "description": "University of Auckland Digital & Lifecycle Content Specialist | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Digital & Lifecycle Content Specialist Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60019814 UoA Department Name: Marketing and Recruitment Job Description Join a newly established team dedicated to deepening customer relationships and driving long-term commercial growth for UOA. Enjoy hybrid work, a 37.5-hour week, and inclusive benefits designed to support wellbeing and caring commitments With more than 47,000 students and over 6,000 staff, Waipapa Taumata Rau, the University of Auckland is Aotearoa New Zealand's leading university and a globally connected organisation dedicated to creating knowledge, transforming lives and shaping the future. As part of a newly established Marketing & Recruitment operating model, our Business Partnering team sits at the centre of strategic decision-making, helping faculties, research institutes and service divisions connect organisational priorities with meaningful marketing and recruitment outcomes. Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity The Digital & Lifecycle Content Specialist (known internally as Digital and Content Specialist) is responsible for the development and delivery of personalised, omnichannel customer lifecycle programs that drive meaningful business results. This is a great opportunity for someone who thrives where creativity, data, and martech intersect. As a key member of the Digital & Performance team, you will work closely with Marketing, Recruitment, Insight and Operations to translate business priorities into clear, actionable plans that directly impact the bottom line. About the role: Act as the Subject Matter Expert (SME) for Customer Lifecycle Management within Marketing and Recruitment, elevating stakeholder understanding and demonstrating clear bottom-line impact. Take end-to-end ownership of lifecycle activities within your assigned portfolio—developing, managing, and continuously optimizing campaigns to align with overarching strategy. Act as the guardian of the CLM strategic frameworks, ensuring compliance across all campaign executions. Collaborate with external agencies and internal teams (digital, marketing, and operations) to deliver cohesive, data-driven, and frictionless customer experiences. Build scalable campaign assets, including landing pages, reusable templates, and content frameworks, to support efficient delivery. Monitor and report on performance, extracting actionable insights that directly drive business OKRs. Maintain strict compliance with local and global privacy and data governance regulations, embedding a privacy-first approach across all touchpoints. This is a full-time, permanent opportunity. The full salary range for this role is $87,000 - $118,000 (Band [G]). We have a structured salary framework with three zones for those developing into the role (developing), fully effective (target) and contributing beyond what is expected of the role (upper). Appointments are typically made within the target range of $87,000 – $107,000 , depending on skills, experience, and internal equity. We welcome conversations about your expectations and what matters to you in your overall package. Any offer will be made within the advertised range and guided by fairness, consistency, and our commitment to pay equity . For more detailed information about the role and requirements, please refer to the Position Description . He kōrero mōu | About you You’re a marketing professional with a minimum of 5 years’ experience developing and delivering effective omnichannel CLM campaigns, leveraging multiple martech platforms. You’re passionate about and have a sound understanding of CLM as a core discipline to delivering hyper-personalisation at scale, and can translate campaign reports into actionable insights and plans. You’re also poised under pressure, highly organised and enjoy solving problems in a fast-paced multistakeholder environment. Whether you’re supporting your manager in developing a new strategy, optimising workflows, or analysing performance, you take a detail-oriented, privacy-first, and customer-focused approach. You enjoy working collaboratively and embrace digital tools and new ways of working to achieve business objectives. What you’ll bring to the role: Sound CLM & CRO Knowledge: An intuitive grasp of customer lifecycle management and CRO principles, with demonstrated experience applying them successfully in complex environments. Hands-on Campaign Execution: Proven capability to design, build, test, and optimise scalable automated campaigns, workflows, and digital touchpoints. Martech Proficiency: Hands-on experience with CRM, CDP, and marketing automation platforms (such as Salesforce Marketing Cloud, Eloqua, or similar enterprise tools). Data & Insights Focus: A results-driven, curious mindset with strong analytical skills to dig into performance data, uncover insights, and drive continuous optimisation. Technical Problem-Solving: The curiosity and technical capability to explore new platform capabilities, troubleshoot blockers, and improve system efficiency. Stakeholder & Influence Skills: Strong communication, presenting and interpersonal skills to manage multiple priorities, collaborate across teams, and advocate for strategy effectively. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer This is a rare opportunity to contribute to a new function, vision and culture while working within an organisation that operates at a significant scale. This new function gives you access to internal expertise and resources commensurate with our complexity and commitments, including an in-house design studio and media production teams, audience specialist teams, web and digital teams, AI and automation expertise, and Māori and Pacific specialists across brand, media, comms and engagement. As a comprehensive university, our scale creates opportunities that few organisations can offer. Whether your interests lie in education, research, innovation, reputation building, community engagement or student growth, you'll have the chance to contribute across a wide range of portfolios, projects and strategic priorities while continuing to grow your own career. Beyond the work itself, you'll be joining a vibrant and inclusive community. From staff networks and cultural communities to social clubs, volunteering opportunities, wellbeing initiatives and campus events, there are countless ways to connect, contribute and build meaningful relationships across the University. We also offer: A commitment to work/life balance with a 37.5 hour working week, flexible hours and hybrid/remote working patterns, as well as discounted public Transport for permanent and long-term fixed term staff A competitive remuneration package with up to 6.75% super, annual salary increase with performance-based multiplier Time to recharge and disconnect with 5 weeks' annual leave and additional leave buy/sell scheme Support for parents and carers with subsidised on-site childcare (including Kōhanga Reo), gender-neutral parental leave up to 9 weeks’ full pay, on-site parenting and feeding spaces A commitment to the wellbeing of our people with confidential access to a range of EAP services, including mental health counselling, financial guidance, neurodiversity coaching and rongoā services, a world-class on-site fitness centre, access to student specialists across our supervised training clinics, discounted health insurance The opportunity to grow with access to an extensive programme of professional, leadership and cultural development, including digital capability coaching, specialised leadership development programmes, and Te Ao and Te Reo Māori learning programmes for staff The opportunity to build your career with one of Aotearoa’s most diverse and complex organisations Find out more about the ways we are transforming how we engage with our internal and external audiences across our Marketing, Recruitment, Communications and Engagement functions. Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Please submit an application online by the closing date of Friday, 16 October 2026 . Please include your cover letter and your CV highlighting your interest in the role, your capabilities and relevant experience. Please reach out to Neil Gardner, Senior Recruitment Consultant, at [email protected] with any questions. Reasonable accommodations - We are committed to building a more equitable and inclusive workforce and workplace, so we encourage applicants to reach out to discuss any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process, including alternative ways to submit applications. Whānau and support people - Should you be invited to an interview for this role, your whānau members and/or support people will be welcome to join you. The recruiter or hiring manager will provide more information about this as part of the interview arrangements. Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000151521319": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "University of Auckland Lecturer/Senior Lecturer - Economics | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Lecturer/Senior Lecturer - Economics Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 55565088 UoA Department Name: Economics Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland creates globally transformative impacts through its distinctive strengths in world-leading research, scholarship, teaching and collaborative partnerships, inspired by its unique position in Aotearoa New Zealand and the Asia-Pacific. The University is Aotearoa New Zealand’s leading higher education institution and a comprehensive, research-intensive university encompassing six diverse faculties and two research institutes. With more than 7,500 students, the Triple Crown accredited University of Auckland Business School is one of the largest and most successful in the Australasian region. The University of Auckland's position in the top 100 of the 2026 QS World Universities Ranking (65th globally, 1st in New Zealand) confirms both its status as New Zealand's pre-eminent research-led university and its place amongst the top 1% of universities worldwide. The University of Auckland Business School has an unconditional commitment to quality teaching and research in topics that are forward-focused and relevant to the commercial world today. The Department offers comprehensive undergraduate, postgraduate, and PhD programmes. Faculty members are active in publishing in leading international peer-reviewed journals, attracting external grants, supervising doctoral students, and maintaining links with the profession, industry, and government. Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We are seeking Lecturers who demonstrate strong research potential, as well as a commitment to excellent research-informed teaching that is enhanced by appropriate learning technologies. Continuation (tenure) is based on performance in research, teaching, and service. In addition to growing your academic profile and reputation, you will also be committed to shaping and delivering an exceptional learning experience for students, contributing to an innovative teaching environment using a variety of methods. We invite applications from candidates in any field but are particularly interested in applicants whose work explores areas including Econometrics (Theoretical and Applied) and International Trade. He kōrero mōu | About you The successful appointee will have a PhD (or be near completion), with demonstrated excellence in research and a commitment to high quality research-informed teaching. You will have a research program that complements and builds upon existing areas of strength within the Department. You will be a highly effective teacher of both undergraduate and graduate students. The appointee will be expected to teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in their specialist area, at introductory levels more widely, and to engage in research and publication both personally and through the supervision of research students. You will also be expected to seek research funding, to engage with the profession and academic and non-academic stakeholders, and to contribute to departmental service. Flexibility in teaching and research collaboration within and beyond the Department are essential. All applications should provide the selection committee with: A cover letter and curriculum vitae Any teaching evaluations Job market paper This is a full time, 40 hours per week, permanent employment contract . The salary ranges are (per annum salary depending on experience and qualifications): The full remuneration range is: Lecture step 1: $99,788 – Lecture step 7: $119,204, depending on qualifications and experience Senior Lecturer - $126,800 - $158,900 NZD, depending on qualifications and experience For more detailed information on the role accountabilities and requirements, please review this position description. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading university and maintains significant computational, laboratory and analytic facilities. Auckland itself is frequently rated as one of the world’s most liveable cities. The University is committed to providing an excellent working environment through: Flexible employment practices (including working from home, flexible hours) Up to 6.75% company superannuation scheme A competitive salary with five weeks’ annual leave Research and study leave In addition, we also offer career development programmes, discounted car parking, a generous parental leave allowance, childcare and a number of other discounts on internal and external services. For more information please visit Staff Benefits . Additional Information Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply All applications must provide the selection committee with: A cover letter and curriculum vitae Any teaching evaluations Full publication record Job market paper Applications must be submitted online, by the closing date of 26th October 2026 (NZ time) to be considered. Please highlight how you can meet the skills and experiences detailed above. Please reach out to Prasanna Gai - Head of Department Economics via [email protected] for a confidential conversation. Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. #LI-DNI Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    }
  },
